
h1. Global PIS / Pay by Bank
h2. System Design Document (SDD)

⸻

h2. 1. Executive Summary

h3. 1.1 Objective

The objective of this initiative is to migrate JPM’s Pay by Bank / Payment Initiation Services (PIS) platform from a custom, single-tenant Tink deployment (Jersey) to Tink’s standard multi-tenant environment (Oxford).

This migration is driven by:
	•	Reduction of vendor cost and bespoke customisations
	•	Adoption of native Tink APIs only
	•	Clear separation of responsibilities between JPM and Tink
	•	Long-term platform scalability and vendor independence

This effort is not a net-new PIS build, but a controlled unpicking and replacement of legacy vendor-specific functionality.

⸻

h3. 1.2 Key Outcomes
	•	Eliminate JPM-specific Tink custom components
	•	JPM owns settlement, reconciliation, refunds, UI, and orchestration
	•	Tink limited to bank connectivity and payment initiation
	•	Stable client-facing APIs with no breaking changes
	•	Clear contract and cost boundaries for vendor negotiation

⸻

h2. 2. Scope

h3. 2.1 In Scope
	•	Migration to Tink multi-tenant (Oxford)
	•	PISP V2 APIs only
	•	Native Tink PIS and AIS APIs
	•	JPM-owned:
	•	Payment orchestration (Kratos)
	•	Settlement and reconciliation
	•	Closed-loop refunds
	•	Client-facing UI and redirects
	•	Webhooks and reporting
	•	Migration activities:
	•	V1 → V2 PIS
	•	Jersey → Oxford
	•	MSFT AIS and Global AIS

⸻

h3. 2.2 Out of Scope
	•	SDK integrations
	•	Auto-refund logic
	•	New V1 functionality
	•	Material changes to existing client-facing APIs

⸻

